Z||000004||Songman||10-26-2000||08:09 PM||||No matter what industry you are in it is the same... I say the same thing about country music. People complain that the music is not as good as it used to be but they keep on buying it, even though the prices are inflated. Why would the labels change? If people would stop buying the crap, and radio would stop playing it.. then the labels would start putting out good music again. They'd have to or they would die...<P>Same with gas prices... $1.51 in Nashville now for regular unleaded.. as long as we keep buying it, they will keep on raising the price... of course, no one has found another source for this yet... we can still find good music on the internet!<P>And of course, the gov't is a big part of the blame on that gas price thing.. but that is another thread altogether..<BR>||||reg||1
