Z||000013||Raydar||10-27-2000||10:38 PM||||RaeQuan, <BR>I look at the controller/software thing a bit differently. The fact that all the old stuff works with the new console will make some folks more likely to go and buy it, just because they <I>can</I> still use the old stuff. Some of the folks at work say that <I>just the processor</I> in the new console costs more than $300. Sony is probably <I>losing</I> money on the console.<BR>Where they are going to make all their profits is with the sales of the new software. What's it cost to mass-produce a game DVD? Maybe $5-10? What are they going to sell for? $50? How many games do most gamers want? All they can get their hands on! <BR>Just my $.02. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>"If I have to fake 'genuine concern' one more time today, I'm gonna scream!" -TCH||||reg||1
